A||||7||Loki||Auto tranny question||||1||
Z||000000||Loki||05-08-2001||09:14 AM||||Well, I was dumb and thought a a leak I had from the cooling lines at the radiator was small...Boy was I wrong....Ina 100 mile drive I had to add 3 quarts..Ewwwwww..But dont think all is lost. This morning I tightned the connection down and added some more tranny fluid...And it seems to be holding and driving fine. Now my question, how many quarts should it hold? 86SE Auto V6<P><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998<BR>www.cox-internet.com/fiero  !!!UPDATED!!!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Wolfhound||05-08-2001||09:28 AM|||| after pan removal..................4 quarts<BR> after overhaul.....................6 quarts<BR> after overhaul and converter drain 9 quarts ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Loki||05-08-2001||09:54 AM||||Cool thanx,<BR>Now then what if I dont remove pan? 3?<BR><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998<BR>www.cox-internet.com/fiero  !!!UPDATED!!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||05-08-2001||01:45 PM||||Check your fluid with the motor hot, idling in Park. Should be in the "operating range" on the dipstick. Add fluid about a half-pint at a time until it comes up to where it should be. <BR>Then shift the tranny through all of it's operating ranges and back to Park. <BR>Check fluid again. The dipstick is right above the shift cable, next to the trunk wall.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 black Formula<BR>88 Duke coupe <BR>88 "wadded up" Formula (parts car)||||reg||1
Z||000004||Loki||05-08-2001||01:56 PM||||Done checked and re checked..Everything seems ok..Drove around for a few hours today.No tranny slippage and drives fine  *WHEW*!!!!!!..THought I had screwed it bad this time..THANX<BR><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998<BR>www.cox-internet.com/fiero  !!!UPDATED!!!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Wolfhound||05-08-2001||02:11 PM||||What Radar said, there is no drain on the Auto. Pulling the pan is the only way to change fluid. Keep an eye on the fluid level and watch for leaks. Tightening may or may not stop the leak. It may require a new gasket if so change the filter. <BR>My 84 failed to unlock this morning exiting the interstate, it did it twice more in town. Looks like I get to replace the lockup solenoid. Oh, Joy!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Loki||05-08-2001||02:36 PM||||Never touched the back of the car except to add and check fluid..Pan is still..The leak was at the radiator where the cooling lines go in and out...No more leaks......   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998<BR>www.cox-internet.com/fiero  !!!UPDATED!!!||||reg||1
Z||000007||Wolfhound||05-08-2001||04:34 PM||||Great, Sorry Loki I,ve read so much about transmissions today I lost track, the solenoid will be here tomorrow so guess thats my duty for tommorrow. ||||reg||7
